  "final_response": "When `git archive` creates an archive, it scans files that have the **`export-subst`** attribute and runs Git’s log‑format processor on the portions of those files that are wrapped in **`$Format:…$`**. It uses **`git log`**’s custom formatter (`pretty=format:`) to expand the format string (e.g., `%cd`, `%aN`, `%h`, `%B`) and replaces the `$Format:…$` markers with the resulting text, then strips the surrounding **`$Format:`** and **`$`** markup. This enables keyword‑expansion processing to be applied to selected parts of the files. The substituted content is written into the archive, producing a file that contains the formatted metadata. The resulting archive is suitable for deployment work but is not suitable for further development work.  \n\n`git archive` …  \n\n[attributes.008-export-subst]",
